+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Flask's default Jinja autoescape selector only recognizes lowercase template
+suffixes, so templates such as `invoice.HTML` and `diagram.SvG` render without
+the protection provided to their lowercase equivalents. Template filenames are
+commonly case-insensitive at the extension level, and this discrepancy is
+surprising and unsafe.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Make Flask's default Jinja autoescape selection recognize its supported
+  template extensions regardless of filename case.
+- Preserve existing behavior for unsupported extensions and unnamed templates.
+- Add regression coverage for uppercase and mixed-case supported extensions.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `template-autoescape`: Default autoescaping decisions for Flask template
+  filenames.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+This affects `Flask.select_jinja_autoescape` in `src/flask/sansio/app.py` and
+the templating tests. No public API signatures or dependencies change.
